US sailors and Marines streamed into the Thai resort city of Pattaya Thursday after a record-breaking nine months at sea. Local police said there had so far been no major incidents connected to the 5,000-strong contingent of US service members, though two sailors were sent back to the ship after a drunken bar brawl.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc92066-a829-11f1-87f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T151123Z-151811266-RC2MBNAFAEVC-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-THAILAND-USA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc92066-a829-11f1-87f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T151123Z-151811266-RC2MBNAFAEVC-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-THAILAND-USA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">36c85f46-a829-11f1-ac16-dbecab1efb8a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 07:02:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc92066-a829-11f1-87f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T151123Z-151811266-RC2MBNAFAEVC-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-THAILAND-USA.jpg">© Chalinee Thirasupa, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>PSG look for their first Ligue 1 win against Monaco</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260904-psg-look-for-their-first-ligue-1-win-against-monaco</link><description>
PSG have still not won a Ligue 1 match this season. After two games, the European champions have recorded two draws. The exact opposite is true of Monaco, who, with two wins from two games, are one of the teams in form at the start of the season. The two Ligue 1 heavyweights will meet on Friday in Paris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4dba2eca-a827-11f1-851f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6CA6L9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4dba2eca-a827-11f1-851f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6CA6L9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">324da5ae-a827-11f1-b613-dbecab1efb8a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 06:23:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Pragmatic international relations': Sánchez seeks to avoid 'further conflict with Rabat'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-pragmatic-international-relations-s%C3%A1nchez-seeks-to-avoid-further-conflict-with-rabat</link><description>
Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Alana Moceri, International Relations Professor at IE School of Politics, Economics and Global Affairs. The migrant crossings at Ceuta have become both a domestic and international political lightning rod. At home, Pedro Sánchez faces opponents who can cast migration in existential terms, with Spain's far right amplifying the rhetoric of "invasion." Internationally, the crisis exposes the geopolitical leverage inherent in control of the border. Ceuta thus emerges as more than a migration crisis: the border becomes at once an instrument of geopolitical leverage, a weapon in Spain's domestic political contest, and a battleground for competing narratives and disinformation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86909780-a817-11f1-82c6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-151203-151949-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86909780-a817-11f1-82c6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-151203-151949-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8c3140fe-a817-11f1-a50b-2b9d0e10922a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 05:22:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
